<!--Post: 6050--><!--Time: 1107495179-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6050"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dorothy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dorothy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 9:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->KAKE video is up <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1228902.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1228902.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6050-->
<!--Post: 6372--><!--Time: 1107732304-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6372"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 3:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If the picture BTK showed Steve back then was really Vian, wouldn&#39;t have LE been contacted before now to investigate? I would have thought that whenever Steve recognized the pic his grandmother or whoever would have contacted LE. I&#39;m not saying I don&#39;t believe Steve, I&#39;m just thinking that surely in all these years LE could have confirmed this and perhaps sought a greater connection between Vian and her killer.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6372-->
<!--Post: 6407--><!--Time: 1107757467-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6407"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 06, 2005 - 10:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->See &#39;Definate victim Shirley Vian&#39; under &#39;Vian&#39;s neighbor Cheryl&#39;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6407-->
<!--Post: 6420--><!--Time: 1107776876-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6420"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 3:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think the child gave reliable testimony. <BR> <BR>Since the Vian son&#39;s interview - he claims that the photo shown him - was the one of he, as a baby, and his mother. <BR> <BR>Yet, he claims he answered the man who asked, with the reply that he did not know the subjects in the picture.  He would have known his mother.   <BR> <BR>And, if it WAS his mother - than BTK was looking for his family - NOT simply targeting them after another gal was not home. <BR> <BR>Don&#39;t put too much stock in the Vian boy&#39;s statement.  It is almost certainly wrong.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6420-->
<!--Post: 6421--><!--Time: 1107778094-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6421"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Raidar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Raidar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 4:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->New at this so please be gentle...I was wondering if they have tried to hypnotize the Vain boy to see if he could remember anything else.I know i aint a cop or nothing but i have seen it on Court TV and A&amp;E before.Just a thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6421-->
<!--Post: 6453--><!--Time: 1107801165-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6453"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Redhead<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Redhead<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 10:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone know what happened to Richard Vian, <BR>Shirley&#39;s husband?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6453-->
<!--Post: 6476--><!--Time: 1107812469-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6476"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lazysean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lazysean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 07, 2005 - 1:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy -- you say &#34;He would have known his mother&#34; -- but I&#39;m not so sure.  We have now seen several different photos of Shirley, all taken within a roughly 5 to 10 year period and none of them seem to look anything like the others!  I think it&#39;s very understandable for a 5 year old child to not immediately recognize an older photo, even of his own mother, unless that picture or one very similar to it was displayed around the home. <BR> <BR>Same goes for recognizing himself in the photo -- sure to us it looks just like him, but I wouldn&#39;t expect a 5 year old to recognize themselves as an infant unless they had seen the photo before. <BR> <BR>Another possibility, though perhaps far-fetched:  it seems Stephen&#39;s grandmother is the source of the info identifying the photo, what if she was simply mistaken?  Meaning what if the kid in the photo is not Stephen but his older brother?  Might be an easy mistake to make, especially if she was telling this to Stephen years later -- and could date the photo even older making Stephen&#39;s story about not recognizing it that much more believable...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6476-->
